# A guard, not a build input. Nothing is meant to be built from this directory.
#
# The one image in this repository takes its own project directory as context --
# `poketrack/` -- and that has its own .dockerignore that is the real one. This
# file exists for the mistake it cannot catch: running
# `docker build -f poketrack/Dockerfile .` from here instead of from
# poketrack/.
#
# Without this, that command uploads every project as build context --
# including any untracked node_modules, which run to hundreds of MB --
# and only then fails on a COPY that is not there. The failure is loud either
# way; this keeps it from being slow and from heating the daemon first.
*/node_modules
*/*/node_modules
*/.venv
*/*/.venv
*/dist
*/*/dist
*/build
*/*/build
*/.next
*/*/.next
.git
